# Line endings: LF in the repository, native in the working tree.
#
# Windows checkouts still get CRLF working copies (core.autocrlf=true handles
# that); this only pins what git STORES. Until now the convention held by habit
# alone, which made it a trap: style.css happened to be stored with CRLF, so
# editing it through a tool that writes LF - then a normal `git add`, which
# normalizes - rewrote all 3800 lines and produced a whole-file diff for a
# 78-line change (2026-07-25). With `text=auto` the stored form no longer
# depends on which editor or script touched the file last.
* text=auto

# Never transform these bytes. PNG data can contain 0x0D0A sequences that mean
# nothing about lines, and "normalizing" them would corrupt the image.
*.png binary
